WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.480
I’m here at the Ashley-Rakahuri Estuary,

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.280
its home to a lot of rare and endangered birds

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.540
and it's a very special place for our district.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.920
The Northern Pegasus Bay Bylaw recognises its importance

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.580
and while everyone is still able to enjoy its natural beauty

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.560
there are rules in place to protect this area.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.620
All visitors need to be careful of the birds and their nesting areas

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.360
you should observe from a distance and leave them undisturbed.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.840
Vehicles, dogs, horses and land yachts aren’t allowed in the Estuary

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.200
If you’re walking past to get to the beach or on a nearby stopbank

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.280
it’s best to keep your dog on its lead.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.480
And let’s leave the airspace to the birds

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.160
so no flying microlights, drones or model aircraft above the Estuary.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.280
It’s all common-sense

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.120
let’s take care of our birds and their home.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.720
We’ve all got a part to play in preserving our beaches and estuary.

